      "why": "Two armored blocks, cracked in two different ways. The red magnet at R3C4 drags the blue shell from the left edge (R3C1) into R3C4, straight above the counter-clockwise spinner P at R6C4, which cracks it - but only if Y at R4C4 has left that column first: otherwise the magnet's own escape turns Y to face down, head-to-head with P. The purple shell at R5C6 is cracked by the spinner P at R5C2, but only after a small chain has turned it to face right: P at R4C1 leaves, which turns Y at R5C1 to face down; Y leaves, which turns P at R5C2 to face right. Only then may the green magnet at R1C6 pull the (now unshelled) purple block up into the top row, where it leaves. Every winning line uses a pull-then-ram (checked exhaustively); only 1 of the 5 legal first moves keeps the board solvable.",
